{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531741-bsds-in-w5","id":1531741,"title":"BSDs in W5","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-29T13:46:00-08:00","id":1531741,"title":"BSDs in W5","content":"In all of the W5 hullabaloo, one thing hasn't truly been discussed in depth.<br /> <br /> What garou being able to breed with other garou and produce fertile offspring means when it comes to BSDs.<br /> <br /> For those coming to this from W5, unless the way BSDs are written is changed drastically, BSDs in Legacy mostly lived in underground caerns called Hives. Because they were underground, Hives often had no need to uphold the veil and since BSDs had very little scruples they would breed with other garou freely. Hence why most of their shock troops were garou born. BSDs also had a habit of stealing the kinfolk of other tribes to be used for further increase their numbers.<br /> <br /> One of the things holding BSDs back in legacy was that garou born were sterile, so they could not utterly outbreed the gaians.<br /> <br /> This is no longer the case in W5. Now there is nothing stopping the BSDs from outnumbering the Gaians by a significant amount.<br /> <br /> Given the focus on CoF, it seems like most of the lore on BSDs will remain Legacy until further notice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-29T14:37:59-08:00","id":1531745,"title":"","content":"If we just look at the W5 corebook, I think there are two sides to BSD: On one hand, you have them as Wyrm-tainted horror-versions of Garou and on the other hand, you have... BSD as punks (in the pejorative sense) who are mean, cause chaos and are spiteful.<br /> <br /> The first part is about how they're these mutated versions of Garou who have fallen to the Wyrm. You still have the same story with the White Howlers - except now that either happened somewhere between the dawn of history or as late as the 18th century. Another case of who knows as a crutch for worldbuilding... You also get this description: &quot;Their bodies have been tortured into shapes resembling bats, feral dogs, rats, and even things unspeakable, as much as they resemble wolves. And though they still possess the ability to change shape, as do Gaian Garou, those shapes are hideous and unnatural.&quot; (pg 277) So the BSD as Garou who have fallen to the Wyrm is there.<br /> <br /> But there's another side to this as well. I think there's a second strain here. It's the BSD as ne'er-do-well punks. That side comes out in the archetype-examples, for example, when the description for the Lurking Scout says &quot;The Lurking Scout loves nothing so much as delivering a blow from the shadows that goes unretaliated.\u200b&quot; or the Caern Raider &quot;Caern Raiders rarely act alone; in the age of Apocalypse, packs of them, large and small, are the scourge of young Garou who devote their own efforts to finding and restoring the caerns that have fallen dormant or been corrupted. No surprise, then, that Caern Raiders take their own malicious glee in once again dragging them to ruin, with as much collateral damage and bloodshed as possible, or befouling them into their own caerns of depravity and rot.\u200b&quot; * This paints a picture of BSD being petty and cowardly. Rather than making an effort to destroy every last caern, they take delight in ruining young Garou's plans to reawaken caerns or they only seek battle when it can't be traced back to them. And then there's of course the Loresheet called &quot;The Black Spiral&quot; where your Garou-PC somehow has contacts in the &quot;Wyrm-scene&quot; and knows about their &quot;hangout-spots&quot; (with the ultimate ability being that you can talk a BSD-member out of being a fan of the Wyrm/&quot;help them emancipate themselves&quot;)<br /> <br /> * I could picture the Dirgesinger as a manipulative Wyrmtongue-style manipulator who veils their lies in so-called prophecies. But the game as a whole is on the same wavelength as the Dirgesinger. The end is nigh and that's it. Period. Not much manipulation left when this Dirgesinger-character is just stating the obvious...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-29T20:45:21-08:00","id":1531767,"title":"","content":"I don't believe that in W5, breeding between garou will always produce another garou. It's important that in W5, nobody really knows how garou are produced. There is no longer the concept of kinfolk, and how garou are born doesn't seem to be purely genetic like it was in the prior editions. So two BSD's having a bunch of kids are most likely going to be having (fucked up) normal human kids rather than an army of other garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T00:45:54-08:00","id":1531769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531741-bsds-in-w5?p=1531767#post1531767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe that in W5, breeding between garou will always produce another garou. It's important that in W5, nobody really knows how garou are produced. There is no longer the concept of kinfolk, and how garou are born doesn't seem to be purely genetic like it was in the prior editions. So two BSD's having a bunch of kids are most likely going to be having (fucked up) normal human kids rather than an army of other garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, but given BSDs are ALL about the numbers game, they'd still outpace the Gaians.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T02:55:13-08:00","id":1531773,"title":"","content":"When it comes to &quot;breeding&quot; in W5, I think there are two areas where you get new werewolves. One is to watch all the bloodlines that have Garou in them. It isn't a surefire thing but being related to a Garou is one reason for why one might become a Kin. And the other is the whole Kinseeking-practice of Garou looking for Kin that just pop up in the world. I think WtF does a better job of explaining this dynamic because the text in the W5 corebook is always written from the perspective of Garou doing the Kinseeking, finding the Kin and then introducing them to their Pack, Tribe and so on and so forth. What's missing is that similarly to how Uratha and the Pure are competing in WtF over newly changed werewolves, I'd imagine you have a similar scenario in W5 now where Kin pop up and Gaian Garou, Cult of Fenris and BSD compete over who that new werewolf joins.<br /> <br /> Personally, I would change the torture/brainwashing-thing from Deepest of Wounds to be the edge the BSD have in recruiting Kin. And meanwhile, the edge the Cult has in recruiting is that with their perspective/philosophy they can evangelize to all the disaffected, cynical and beaten-down Garou (who may be on the verge of succumbing to Harano or are already in the thrall of Hauglosk) and get them to switch sides rather than the Cult actually doing Kinseekings of their own. But that's how I would do it. The W5 corebook doesn't really get into that aspect of Kinseekings and Deepest of Wounds of course assigns torture/brainwashing to be a Cult of Fenris thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T07:11:51-08:00","id":1531781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531741-bsds-in-w5?p=1531769#post1531769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep, but given BSDs are ALL about the numbers game, they'd still outpace the Gaians.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe? I get the feeling that in W5, most Garou end up being &quot;foundlings&quot; - random people who turn into werewolves and are then found and recruited by the tribes. So if BSD's just focused on breeding and not going out and looking for people, then the Gaian werewolves would end up with bigger numbers because the vast, vast majority of BSD kids would just be regular people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T07:20:49-08:00","id":1531782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531741-bsds-in-w5?p=1531773#post1531773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'd imagine you have a similar scenario in W5 now where Kin pop up and Gaian Garou, Cult of Fenris and BSD compete over who that new werewolf joins.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you are missing out the horror of what I'm implying. The BSDs can just breed freely and any non-Kin is a useful servant/food. In addition they can of course try to capture non-related kin. But there is no longer as much of a need to seek bloodlines outside the Hive.<br /> <br /> And hey, wolf-born are a thing. Litters mean more chances for Kin.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T13:16:35-08:00","id":1531799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531741-bsds-in-w5?p=1531767#post1531767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe that in W5, breeding between garou will always produce another garou. It's important that in W5, nobody really knows how garou are produced. There is no longer the concept of kinfolk, and how garou are born doesn't seem to be purely genetic like it was in the prior editions. So two BSD's having a bunch of kids are most likely going to be having (fucked up) normal human kids rather than an army of other garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet somehow we have a whole tribe based on bloodlines and lineages...<br /> <br /> I do feel that the W5 version of BSD's is rather half baked. The book posits that they have won and leaves them rather directionless, and in places where we should consider that they are the biggest threat to the Garou, we are now finding the Cult of Fenris as the key antagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 03-01-2024, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T17:51:46-08:00","id":1531825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531741-bsds-in-w5?p=1531799#post1531799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yet somehow we have a whole tribe based on bloodlines and lineages...</div> </div> </div> </div>And ancestors and other stuff. There's a lot of stuff in W5 that's a mess. I'm just pointing out what the official stance on the game is, dumb as it might be. Breeding new werewolves won't work in W5 because that's not how Werewolves work anymore, and of course, nobody knows how they work so all we can do is sit in the dark and throw darts at the wall.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T17:59:06-08:00","id":1531828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531741-bsds-in-w5?p=1531782#post1531782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you are missing out the horror of what I'm implying. The BSDs can just breed freely and any non-Kin is a useful servant/food. In addition they can of course try to capture non-related kin. But there is no longer as much of a need to seek bloodlines outside the Hive.<br /> <br /> And hey, wolf-born are a thing. Litters mean more chances for Kin.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm inclined to agree, the more humans and wolves they accumulate the better their chances of a Garou arising in their midst and its not like a horde of Delirium affected/resistant mind-shattered humans armed with silver don't make a somewhat lower powered replacement for a bunch of insane Warborn as an attack force.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T19:37:46-08:00","id":1531834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531741-bsds-in-w5?p=1531782#post1531782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you are missing out the horror of what I'm implying. The BSDs can just breed freely and any non-Kin is a useful servant/food. In addition they can of course try to capture non-related kin. But there is no longer as much of a need to seek bloodlines outside the Hive.<br /> <br /> And hey, wolf-born are a thing. Litters mean more chances for Kin.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right but there's a reason why I hadn't considered this and it applies to Kin in general in W5, I would say. WtF does a better job of doing this by introducing Wolf-Blooded and giving them a bigger role in Packs. Since W5 kept the &quot;You become a Kin because you're related to a Garou&quot;-bit in the game, the path we're following here is just a circuitous route to re-inventing the wheel, specifically we're talking here about bringing back Kinfolk. Both Wolf-Blooded and Kin are replacements for Kinfolk but the former is a far more fleshed-out idea compared to the latter. Kin and who gets to be a werewolf is another area where I think W5 would have benefited from being a bit more radical in being different. Kin feels like a half-measure in coming up with a new take on the Kinfolk-idea.<br /> <br /> Imagine that since any person can become a Kin and then their First Change could happen at any point during their life (maybe as late as in their 50s), there could be a certain number of Kin-hangers-on who for whatever reason are Kin tied to Packs of Garou, Cult of Fenris or BSD but haven't experienced their First Change. This would be Kinfolk with the difference that they could go through their First Change at some point in their lives. But that way you get back the Kinfolk of old.<br /> <br /> Also, Kin must be a step between being a normal person and turning into a werewolf with the First Change. I don't think the W5 corebook covers this, though. One shouldn't be Kin from birth because then Kinseeking would be fairly easy. Just do the Rite near any gathering of young ones (be they humans or wolves) and then you just kidnap the ones who are Kin.<br /> <br /> And of course, you're right that now with the removal of Crinos-born, there are some dark implications as to how evil werewolves like BSD might generate more Kin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T07:30:23-08:00","id":1531882,"title":"","content":"I know I have the reputation as the resident W5 apologist but I'm going to say that doesn't necessarily mean much and could actually work out pretty well.<br /> <br /> Draw from &quot;The Rats in the Wall&quot;, &quot;Texas Chainsaw Massacre&quot;, &quot;Children of the Corn&quot;, and other sorts of crazy monster communities and you have a lot of fun potential to be had there.<br /> <br /> The BSD now come from whole communities of fucked up Wyrm cultists and that works just fine.<br /> <br /> Assuming that you also don't just &quot;cheat&quot; by saying that the Black Spiral Dancers do just breed with one another and the Wyrm guarantees that each child is a Garou because EvilTM can do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T07:41:45-08:00","id":1531885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531741-bsds-in-w5?p=1531882#post1531882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know I have the reputation as the resident W5 apologist but I'm going to say that doesn't necessarily mean much and could actually work out pretty well.<br /> <br /> Draw from &quot;The Rats in the Wall&quot;, &quot;Texas Chainsaw Massacre&quot;, &quot;Children of the Corn&quot;, and other sorts of crazy monster communities and you have a lot of fun potential to be had there.<br /> <br /> The BSD now come from whole communities of fucked up Wyrm cultists and that works just fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, they have always come with whole communities of Wyrm cultists, there is even a camp called Generation Hex which is basically Leatherface's familyx100.<br /> <br /> They now can be even MORE insular than they've been before. Which is scary, because this means you could have GENERATIONS who never see the sunlight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T08:44:34-08:00","id":1531887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531741-bsds-in-w5?p=1531885#post1531885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, they have always come with whole communities of Wyrm cultists, there is even a camp called Generation Hex which is basically Leatherface's familyx100.<br /> <br /> They now can be even MORE insular than they've been before. Which is scary, because this means you could have GENERATIONS who never see the sunlight.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're thinking of the Genetic Irregulars, and they mostly referenced <i>Deliverance</i> (poorly, as the example character misquotes it) over <i>The Texas Chainsaw Massacre</i>. Generation Hex were the tech-savvy corner of the tribe that reached out to people via the internet in really disturbing ways. They were the kind of people who hanged out in 8chan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T09:07:39-08:00","id":1531890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531741-bsds-in-w5?p=1531887#post1531887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're thinking of the Genetic Irregulars, and they mostly referenced <i>Deliverance</i> (poorly, as the example character misquotes it) over <i>The Texas Chainsaw Massacre</i>. Generation Hex were the tech-savvy corner of the tribe that reached out to people via the internet in really disturbing ways. They were the kind of people who hanged out in 8chan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the correction!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T11:45:03-08:00","id":1531965,"title":"","content":"There may actually be some interesting tales to be told with the 5th Edition Black Spiral Dancers, especially if Bat is still a patron spirit with multiple aspects, at least one of which has been brought back to Gaia: if nothing else, it\u2019s interesting to wonder how many clashes there have been between BSDs happy to cry \u201cMission Accomplished!\u201d and those enthusiasts who believe that the minute the Tribe of the Fallen stop fighting the Forces of Gaia start winning.<br /> <br /> This doesn\u2019t even consider those Black Spiral Dancers with a survival instinct strong enough to make them wonder if they actually WANT to die with the Old World, now that the finish line is in sight - what might they do to find an escape hatch, or at least prolong (and possibly improve) their own miserable existence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T04:20:03-08:00","id":1532001,"title":"","content":"This goes under one of those problematic bits of W5. The setting of W5 never was the setting of Legacy, it was always like this, so none of the story elements from before exist, nor has the world developed in a diagetic way. So far the Devs and people on the discord including Outstar have been quite vocal on not including old stuff in W5 because it's &quot;not that kind of game&quot;. It does make me wonder what changed in the past months to show that they are bringing back elements of legacy into W5 and V5 with Shattered Nation and Gehenna Wars. It could be a sign of a major change in direction for both lines. It would also be the devteam going back on their strange stances of how &quot;pure&quot; these games should be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T06:44:30-08:00","id":1532017,"title":"","content":"At this point the most sensible approach is, I suspect, to read these sourcebooks with polite attention and an eye to making what YOU want out of the setting presented, rather than be wedded to one of the less well-thought-of WEREWOLF editions.<br /> <br /> After all, good ideas can hide in the most unexpected places.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T14:23:00-08:00","id":1532113,"title":"","content":"Ah, I see that such optimism is not entirely welcome!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T14:59:41-08:00","id":1532119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531741-bsds-in-w5?p=1532001#post1532001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This goes under one of those problematic bits of W5. The setting of W5 never was the setting of Legacy, it was always like this, so none of the story elements from before exist, nor has the world developed in a diagetic way. So far the Devs and people on the discord including Outstar have been quite vocal on not including old stuff in W5 because it's &quot;not that kind of game&quot;. It does make me wonder what changed in the past months to show that they are bringing back elements of legacy into W5 and V5 with Shattered Nation and Gehenna Wars. It could be a sign of a major change in direction for both lines. It would also be the devteam going back on their strange stances of how &quot;pure&quot; these games should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, aside from W5 not starting out as a reimagining of W:tA, anyway. Most of any celebration about more of legacy cropping up now is more of a schadenfreude situation, though. No telling when it's going to take another hard jerk on the wheel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}